From 3fe3dfe937c67ee26e3a73d514f4ade73f62ec9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:22:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Reconstruct private decoder history after preemption

Base: candidate-38 1f33102547e4da5c64712390604695d1abd577c4, built from upstream 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 and its ordered series.

Recovery keeps the original prompt replay floor and every accepted generated row. The shared encoder prefix cannot skip the private decoder history needed by deeper sliding-window layers. Normal prompt and decode arithmetic is unchanged; recovery deliberately does more work after private state is lost.

Tests: independent group eviction and lifecycle oracle, original-boundary allocation regressions, metadata/reordering cases, and native three-layer TileLang recovery reproducer. CPU cache suite: 395 passed, four known HiSparse cases deselected; 45 isolated policy cases passed. Native GPU and full serving validation remain pending. Upstream status: experimental fork proposal, not submitted upstream or promoted.
